---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: countries
navKey: countries
title: "Countries — the full analytical view — Citere"
description: "The breakdown behind the countries page: coverage, refusals, retrieval, per-assistant and per-claim tables, source locality and the grain-of-truth split."
pagination:
  data: build.languages
  alias: lang
  size: 1
permalink: "{{ '/countries/full/' | loc(lang) }}"
---
{%- from "partials/bot-mark.njk" import botMark -%}
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="{{ '/' | url }}">Home</a> /
  <a href="{{ '/countries/' | url }}">Countries</a> / <span aria-current="page">Full data</span></nav>
<div class="phead"><h1>Countries &mdash; the full analytical view</h1>
  <p class="plead" style="max-width:70ch">The breakdown behind the narrative page: the same pre-computed
    cells, arranged for someone who needs every figure rather than the reading of it. Nothing here is
    averaged across question types, markets or runs.</p></div>

<h2 id="coverage" style="margin:26px 0 6px">1. What has been tested where</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Claims tested per market, with the run and the frozen grid version.
  Comparisons are only made between markets sharing a grid version.</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Claims, runs and versions per market</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Market</th><th scope="col" class="num">Claims</th><th scope="col" class="num">Answers</th>
    <th scope="col">Runs</th><th scope="col">Grid</th><th scope="col">Comparable with</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}
    {%- set pooled = metrics.poolOf({ "run": c.run.key, "is_live": false }) %}
    <tr><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">{{ c.key | flag }} {{ c.name }}</th>
      <td class="num">{{ c.run.claims_count }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ pooled.n }}</td>
      <td style="color:var(--dim);font-size:12.5px">{{ runs.byMarket[c.market] | length }}</td>
      <td style="color:var(--dim)">{{ c.run.versions.grid }}</td>
      <td style="color:var(--dim);font-size:12.5px">{% if c.run.comparable_with | length %}{{ c.run.comparable_with | length }} run(s){% else %}&mdash;{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

{%- for persona in metrics.dimensions.personas %}
<h2 id="rr-{{ persona }}" style="margin:30px 0 6px">Repeat rate &mdash; {{ persona }} {{ persona | personaLabel }}</h2>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat rate per assistant and market at {{ persona }}</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.chatbot' | t }}</th>
    {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}<th scope="col" class="num">{{ c.key | upper }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for bot in countriesReport.chatbots %}
    <tr data-persona="{{ persona }}"><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">{{ bot.name }}</th>
      {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}
      {%- set cell = metrics.poolOf({ "chatbot": bot.key, "run": c.run.key, "persona": persona, "is_live": false }) %}
      <td class="num"><span class="cellstat{% if cell.repeat_rate.low_n %} lown{% endif %}">{{ cell.repeat_rate.rate | rate }}<small>{{ cell.repeat_rate.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ cell.repeat_rate.n }}</small></span></td>
      {%- endfor %}</tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>
{%- endfor %}

<h2 id="silence" style="margin:30px 0 6px">Silence map &mdash; refusals</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Share of answers that were a refusal or an evasion, at the neutral
  question. A market that looks clean because assistants do not answer is not clean.</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Refusal rate per assistant and market at the neutral question</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.chatbot' | t }}</th>
    {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}<th scope="col" class="num">{{ c.key | upper }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for bot in countriesReport.chatbots %}
    <tr data-persona="P1"><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">{{ bot.name }}</th>
      {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}
      {%- set cell = metrics.poolOf({ "chatbot": bot.key, "run": c.run.key, "persona": "P1", "is_live": false }) %}
      <td class="num"><span class="cellstat">{{ cell.dodge_rate.rate | rate }}<small>n={{ cell.dodge_rate.n }}</small></span></td>
      {%- endfor %}</tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

<h2 id="retrieval" style="margin:30px 0 6px">How often assistants searched</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Share of answers containing any citation, at the news-style
  question. This separates "clean because it never looked" from "looked and stayed clean".</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Share of answers citing anything, per assistant and market</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.chatbot' | t }}</th>
    {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}<th scope="col" class="num">{{ c.key | upper }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for bot in countriesReport.chatbots %}
    <tr data-persona="{{ countriesReport.persona }}"><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">{{ bot.name }}</th>
      {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}
      {%- set cell = metrics.poolOf({ "chatbot": bot.key, "run": c.run.key, "persona": countriesReport.persona, "is_live": false }) %}
      <td class="num"><span class="cellstat">{{ cell.retrieval_rate.rate | rate }}<small>listed: {{ cell.contamination_rate.rate | rate }}</small></span></td>
      {%- endfor %}</tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

<h2 id="claims" style="margin:30px 0 6px">One claim, every market</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Repeats per claim per market at the news-style question. Single-claim
  cells at three repeats: direction only.</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Repeats per claim and market</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.claim' | t }}</th><th scope="col">Splice</th>
    {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}<th scope="col" class="num">{{ c.key | upper }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for claim in claims %}{% if claim.tested %}
    <tr><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400" class="cl"><a href="{{ claim.url | url }}">{{ claim.id }}</a>
        <small>{{ claim.label }}</small></th>
      <td><span class="splicebadge sp-{{ claim.splice }}">{{ claim.splice }}</span></td>
      {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}
      {%- set cell = metrics.poolOf({ "claim": claim.id, "run": c.run.key, "persona": countriesReport.persona, "is_live": false }) %}
      <td class="num">{% if cell.counts.repeat %}<b>{{ cell.counts.repeat }}</b>{% else %}<span style="color:var(--dimmer)">0</span>{% endif %}</td>
      {%- endfor %}</tr>
  {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

<h2 id="locality" style="margin:30px 0 6px">Which listed sources are local</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">A domain is local to a market when every recorded citation of it
  came from there. Local sources show where a language-specific mirror exists and works.</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Citations per market for each listed domain</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.domain' | t }}</th><th scope="col">Locality</th>
    {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}<th scope="col" class="num">{{ c.key | upper }}</th>{% endfor %}
    <th scope="col" class="num">Total</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for s in publishedSources %}{% if s.citedCount %}
    <tr><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400"><a href="{{ s.url | url }}"><span class="domain">{{ s.defanged }}</span></a></th>
      <td style="font-size:12.5px;{% if s.markets | length == 1 %}color:var(--false);font-weight:600{% else %}color:var(--dim){% endif %}">
        {%- if s.markets | length == 1 %}local to {{ s.markets[0] | upper }}{% elif s.markets | length >= 3 %}global{% else %}regional{% endif %}</td>
      {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}<td class="num">{{ s.byMarket[c.market] | default(0) }}</td>{% endfor %}
      <td class="num"><b>{{ s.citedCount }}</b></td></tr>
  {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

<h2 id="grain" style="margin:30px 0 6px">Grain-of-truth split by market</h2>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat rate on claims built on a real event against pure fabrications, per market</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Market</th><th scope="col" class="num">Real event underneath</th>
    <th scope="col" class="num">Pure fabrication</th><th scope="col">Difference</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in countriesReport.grain %}
    <tr data-persona="{{ countriesReport.persona }}"><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">{{ row.country.name }}</th>
      <td class="num"><span class="cellstat">{{ row.grain.rate | rate }}<small>{{ row.grain.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ row.grain.n }}</small></span></td>
      <td class="num"><span class="cellstat">{{ row.fabrication.rate | rate }}<small>{{ row.fabrication.ci | ciLabel }} &middot; n={{ row.fabrication.n }}</small></span></td>
      <td style="color:var(--dim);font-size:12.5px">{{ "significant" if row.significant else "not significant" }}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

<h2 id="countermeasures" style="margin:30px 0 6px">Countermeasures by market</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Counts by type. No ratio of countermeasures to incidents: the two
  are not comparable across markets with different amounts of testing.</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Countermeasures per market by type</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Market</th>
    {%- for t in countermeasures.types %}{% if t.count %}<th scope="col" class="num">{{ t.label }}</th>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    <th scope="col">Targets</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for c in countriesReport.countries %}
    {%- set rows = countermeasures.actions | whereEq('market', c.market) %}
    <tr><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400">{{ c.name }}</th>
      {%- for t in countermeasures.types %}{% if t.count %}
      <td class="num">{{ rows | whereEq('displayType', t.key) | length }}</td>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      <td style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--dim)">{% for a in rows | unique('target') | take(3) %}{{ a.target | defangCopy }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if not rows | length %}none yet{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

<div class="exports" style="margin:26px 0 44px">
  <a href="{{ '/countries/' | url }}">Back to the countries page</a>
  {%- if datasets.has['registry-csv'] %}<span>&middot;</span><a href="{{ '/registry.csv' | url }}">Every metric cell as CSV</a>{% endif %}
</div>
